      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e02b10dabcb601455e63632c2ed90bda2b0cda97f843ecc48b90307aa58d0a90",
      "text": "Day 7 · Breakfast, then a 3-hour city tour with an English-speaking guide: the old district of La Boca; San Telmo, with its bars, restaurants and the antiques market of Plaza Dorrego; the Plaza de Mayo and the Casa Rosada, the presidential palace linked to the memory of Eva Perón; the 67-metre Obelisk on Avenida 9 de Julio, one of the widest avenues in the world; elegant Recoleta, with its famous cemetery and the colonial church of El Pilar; and modern Puerto Madero.\n\nEvening · A tango show with dinner (without a guide). Born in the port districts of Buenos Aires among immigrants and gauchos, tango is today one of the most sensual dances in the world; a menu of traditional dishes and excellent Argentine wines completes this romantic evening.",
